# Cursor Rules for {PROJECT_NAME}

- Adhere to Clean Architecture and isolation principles outlined in `docs/architecture/overview.md`.
- Never commit or print real secrets, private keys, or credentials.
- Commit messages must follow Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `test:`).
- Always include automated unit tests alongside code changes.
- Refer to `.agents/rules/coding-rules-general.md` and `.agents/rules/languages/coding-rules-{PRIMARY_LANGUAGE}.md`.
- File naming must strictly follow `.agents/rules/naming-rules-general.md` (agent definitions must end with `*.agent.md`, prefix `agent-` is strictly prohibited).
- Follow the permission tiers in `.agents/rules/permission-rules-general.md` (A: always allow, C: conditional, N: never); `.cursor/cli.json` and `.cursor/permissions.json` enforce them.
- **Output Language**: Reply to the user and write PR titles/descriptions in Japanese; commit messages, code, identifiers, and comments stay in English. Details: `.agents/rules/git-rules-commit.md`.
